I can now call a model with the grammar. I haven't done it locally
yet, but I might be able to create reversed training data this way.
Going to look and see if I can get a good distribution of different
prob models.

A few notes on the grammar:
 - Probabilit handles both probabilistic and deterministic variables
   with the same syntax. The llm does not like this as "normal"
   probabilistic languages seem to use ~ as probabilistic assignment.
   This means that probabilistic variables cannot be used in an
   expression. I don't really see this as a problem and I believe it
   will just be clearer really.
 - It was the model that insisted on adding a return statement. I
   didn't first add it.
 - I am uncertain if it is good to just use the scipy.stats
   distributions directly or if we should let it give the variables
   proper names.

